title: Palo Alto Networks: BGP peer state
agents: paloalto_api
catalog: hw/network/paloalto
license: GPLv2
distribution: checkmk-paloalto-api
description:
 Reports the state of every BGP peer the firewall has configured, read with
 "show routing protocol bgp peer" (or "show advanced-routing bgp peer-status"
 on devices running Advanced Routing). A peer is OK when its session is
 "Established"; the states it passes through on the way up (Idle, Connect,
 Active, OpenSent, OpenConfirm) are WARN by default and anything else is
 CRIT. Both can be changed in the rule "Palo Alto BGP peers", together with
 lower levels on the session uptime, which catches a peer that keeps
 flapping, and on the number of prefixes received.

 PAN-OS does not expose BGP peer state over SNMP, so this has no equivalent
 among the SNMP based checks.

item:
 The peer name as configured on the firewall.

discovery:
 One service per BGP peer. No service is created if BGP is not configured.
